<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Šubašić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1892">1892</a>–<a href="/years/1955">1955</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Šubašić was a Croatian politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-peasant-party">Croatian Peasant Party</a> who served as ban of the autonomous Banovina of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1939 to 1941. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> he went into exile, and in 1944 became prime minister of the Yugoslav government-in-exile, signing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a>–Šubašić agreements with the Partisans. He briefly served as foreign minister of Tito's government before resigning in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-subasic.jpg" alt="Ivan Šubašić" width="170" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SFR Yugoslavia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivan_%C5%A0uba%C5%A1i%C4%87_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
